# spinny-scraper — credentials and defaults
#
# Copy this file to `.env` next to the scripts and fill in what you use:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is in .gitignore. Keep it there. A secret passed on a command line
# is readable by anything that can run `ps` and lands in your shell history,
# which is why none of these has a flag you are expected to type.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#
#     explicit CLI flag  >  exported environment variable  >  .env  >  default
#
# So a `.env` never overrides something you typed, and an already-exported
# variable (a CI secret, direnv, your shell profile) is never clobbered by a
# file you forgot to delete.
#
# Check what was picked up, without printing any secret:
#
#     python3 env_config.py
#
# Every variable below is one this code actually reads, and every variable
# the code reads is below — smoke_test.py asserts the two sets are equal in
# both directions, because a documented-but-unread variable is worse than an
# undocumented one.
#
# The `{...}` placeholders below are treated as UNSET by the loader. That is
# deliberate: a copied example that read as CONFIGURED would connect with the
# literal string `{login}-zone-...` as its username and get a 401 a long way
# from its cause — which happened in four sibling repos at once, because
# their placeholder check was a list of literals and none of them matched a
# credentialled URL written the way the vendor documents it.


# --- 2Captcha -------------------------------------------------------------
# One key, four separately-billed products: captcha solving, the Scraping
# Browser API, proxies and fingerprints. https://2captcha.com
#
# WORTH KNOWING BEFORE YOU BUY SOLVING FOR THIS SITE: it buys nothing here,
# and the reason is more interesting than "no captcha was seen".
#
# Spinny HAS reCAPTCHA configured on every page it serves — 31 occurrences of
# "recaptcha" on a capture that had just delivered 482 cars — but it is
# **Enterprise v3, invisible**, with a badge the site's own CSS hides. v3
# SCORES a session in the background rather than challenging it, so there is
# nothing rendered for a visitor to solve and nothing for a solver to buy. No
# rendered challenge was observed from either exit tested, measured
# 2026-09-11.
#
# The solving path is wired up and capped at one purchase per page, because a
# bot manager can be switched on between deploys and a scraper that cannot
# name what stopped it is much harder to fix. It is not part of the happy
# path. If Spinny ever does start gating the grid on a score, what a key
# would buy is an enterprise v3 score task — the scrapers read that off the
# site's own loader rather than guessing, because v3 parameters sent for a v2
# widget buy a token the site rejects.
#
# This key IS what --fingerprint uses (a separate subscription from solving:
# a working solver key is not automatically enabled for fingerprints, and the
# client says so by name if it is not).
TWOCAPTCHA_KEY=your_2captcha_api_key_here

# --- Scraping Browser API -------------------------------------------------
# A remote browser you do not run or patch, with a persistent profile and a
# chosen exit country. Used by --cdp-endpoint.
#
#   country-  picks the exit country, and on this site it decides very
#             little: an Amsterdam datacentre exit and a Chennai residential
#             exit returned the same page, the same advertised total and INR
#             prices both times (2026-09-11). Spinny sells in one country,
#             has one storefront and does not geo-redirect, so there is no
#             --country flag on the scrapers either. What DOES vary is the
#             city, and the city is part of the URL.
#   pid-      is a profile with persistent cookies. ONE live connection each,
#             capped per account — reuse pids rather than minting one per
#             run, and expect a 500 (`profile_locked`, exit 5) while another
#             run still holds this one. Leave roughly a minute between runs
#             on one pid, and give CI its own.
#
# Note that Selenium cannot use this: chromedriver's `debuggerAddress` takes
# a bare host:port with nowhere to put a password. Playwright and pyppeteer
# authenticate on the WebSocket upgrade and work. selenium_scraper.py refuses
# a credentialed endpoint with exit 2 and says which engine to use instead.
SPINNY_CDP_ENDPOINT=ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-in-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222

# --- Proxy ----------------------------------------------------------------
# One URL here, or --proxy-file with one per line for a pool.
#
# You are unlikely to need one for a single run: no Spinny refusal was ever
# observed, and a bare local Chromium on a plain connection returned the full
# grid with no key and no proxy. What a pool buys is VOLUME from many
# addresses — which is also why `--concurrency` is refused on this site, so a
# pool here spreads several sequential runs rather than parallel ones.
#
# The credentials here never reach the browser's command line — they go
# through the driver's own fields. Logs keep the host and port and mask the
# rest, because which exit a run used is the point of the log and is not the
# secret. Selenium's --proxy-server cannot authenticate at all, so that
# engine strips the credentials and warns rather than letting you believe a
# user:pass URL is doing something.
SPINNY_PROXY=http://{user}:{password}@in.proxy.2captcha.com:2334

# --- Default target -------------------------------------------------------
# Saves retyping --url. Spinny is ONE storefront on ONE hostname serving one
# country in one currency, so there is no locale prefix and no per-country
# hostname to get wrong. The CITY is in the path.
#
# Which URL you pick decides what you get:
#
#   /used-cars-in-{city}/s/       a city listing. ONE infinitely scrolling
#                                 page: ?page=N is silently IGNORED and
#                                 returns page 1 under HTTP 200, so --pages N
#                                 means N batches of 20 cars reached by
#                                 SCROLLING, and --concurrency is refused
#                                 with that reason.
#   /used-{make}-cars-in-{city}/s/    a filtered listing — same shape, and
#   /used-cars-under-{n}-lakh-rs-in-{city}/s/   these ARE separate addresses,
#                                 so several runs across them parallelise
#                                 where --concurrency cannot.
#   /used-cars/s/                 no city in the path. Spinny scopes
#                                 inventory by city, so the grid container is
#                                 served and stays EMPTY: exit 4, and the URL
#                                 rather than a fault.
#   /used-cars                    an SEO landing page with no grid at all.
#                                 Answers 200 and yields zero rows, exit 4.
#   /buy-used-cars/.../{id}/      one car, with --mode detail.
SPINNY_URL=https://www.spinny.com/used-cars-in-delhi-ncr/s/

# Deliberately NOT here: an output prefix. `--out` already carries a
# non-empty default, so the loader — which only fills UNSET values — would
# never see it, and the variable would be silently inert: a setting that
# looks configurable and is not.
